---
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Claudia Cervantes | Portfolio</title>
    <style>
		/* -------------------- */
		/* Global */
		/* -------------------- */
      :root {
        color-scheme: dark;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        background: #0b0b0b;
        color: #f5f5f5;
      }
		/* -------------------- */
		/* Layout */
		/* -------------------- */

	  main {
  		padding: 48px 24px 80px;
	  }
	  .role {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		letter-spacing: 2px;
		color: #7bdcb5;
		margin-bottom: 8px;
	  }
		/* -------------------- */
		/* Hero Section */
		/* -------------------- */  
	  .hero {
  	    padding: 40px 0 20px;
      }

      .container {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        width: 100%;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        color: #b3b3b3;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
        line-height: 1.05;
        margin: 0 0 16px;
      }

      .subtitle {
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: #d0d0d0;
        max-width: 740px;
		line-height: 1.45;
        margin: 0 0 32px;
      }
		/* -------------------- */
		/* Navigation Links */
		/* -------------------- */
      .links {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 12px;
      }

      .links a {
        color: #f5f5f5;
        text-decoration: none;
        border: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
        padding: 10px 16px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        transition: 0.2s ease;
      }

      .links a:hover {
        border-color: #f5f5f5;
      }

	  .lang {
	    font-size: 0.8em;
		opacity: 0.65;
	  }	

	  .links a {
	    font-size: 0.95rem;
	  }

		/* -------------------- */
		/* About Section */
		/* -------------------- */	  
	  .about {
		padding: 35px 0 10px;
	  }

	  .about h2 {
		font-size: 1.8rem;
		margin: 0 0 20px;
	  }

	  .about p {
		max-width: 820px;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.50;
		color: #cfcfcf;
		margin: 0 0 16px;
	  }

		/* -------------------- */
		/* Projects Section */
		/* -------------------- */
	  .projects {
	    padding: 50px 0;
		border-top: 1px solid #222;
	  }

	  .projects h2 {
	    font-size: 2rem;
	    margin-bottom: 32px;
	  }

	  .project-grid {
	    display: grid;
	    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
	    gap: 28px;
	  }

		/* -------------------- */
		/* Project Cards */
		/* -------------------- */

	  .project-card {
	    text-decoration: none;
	    color: inherit;
	    border: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
	    border-radius: 14px;
	    overflow: hidden;
		background: #111
	    transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
	  }

	  .project-card:hover {
	    transform: translateY(-4px);
	    border-color: #3a3a3a;
  		box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
	  }

	  .project-card img {
	    width: 100%;
	    height: 220px;
		object-fit: contain;
	    display: block;
  		background: #111;
		padding: 12px 16px 0;
	  }

	  .project-card h3 {
	    font-size: 1.1rem;
	    padding: 16px 16px 4px;
		margin: 0;
	  }

	  .project-card p {
	    font-size: 0.9rem;
	    color: #c8c8c8;
	    padding: 0 16px 8px;
		margin: 0;
	  }

	  .tools {
  		font-size: 0.8rem;
  		color: #9aa8b5;
  		padding: 0 16px 16px;
		margin: 0;
  		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
	  }

	  @media (max-width: 900px) {
  		.project-grid {
    	  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  		}
	  }

    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="hero">
    	<div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Portfolio</p>
		<p class="role">DATA ANALYTICS</p>
        <h1>Claudia Cervantes</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          Helping organizations transform data into better decisions.
        </p>

        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/claudia-cervantes-worldwide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/cloud9international"" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <a href="/claudia-cervantes-cv-en.pdf" target="_blank">CV <span class="lang">(English)</span></a>
  		  <a href="/claudia-cervantes-cv-es.pdf" target="_blank">CV <span class="lang">(Español)</span></a>
          <a href="mailto:claudia.cervantes.worldwide@gmail.com?subject=Portfolio Contact">Contact</a>
        </div>
		
      	</div>
	    </section>
	  
		<section class="about">
		  <div class="container">
			<h2>About</h2>
			<p>
			I bring a background in CRM, operations, and cross-functional coordination across cultural organizations,
			nonprofits, and government environments into data analytics. My work has always centered on using data
			to make information clearer, improve processes, and support better decision-making.
			</p>
			<p>
			This portfolio reflects my move into modern analytics through hands-on projects in Python, SQL, Power BI,
			Tableau, API integrations, and AWS cloud workflows. From messy HR data audits and global well-being dashboards
			to music data pipelines and interactive Tableau projects, each project helped me build stronger skills in data
			cleaning, exploratory analysis, dashboard design, ETL, and storytelling with data.
			</p>
			<p>
			I’m especially interested in roles where analytics connects technical work with real organizational needs:
			turning complex information into useful insights, automating repetitive work, and helping teams make better
			decisions with data.
			</p>
		  </div>
		</section>

		<section class="projects">
		<div class="container">
		<h2>Selected Projects</h2>

		<div class="project-grid">

		<a class="project-card" href="/projects/aws-cloud-data-pipeline">
			<img src="/projects/aws-cloud-data-pipeline.jpg" alt="AWS serverless analytics pipeline architecture">
			<h3>AWS Cloud Data Pipeline</h3>
			<p>
			Designed an end-to-end serverless data pipeline using AWS to automate data ingestion, ETL, 
			cataloging, and SQL-based analysis.
			</p>
			<p class="tools">AWS · S3 · Lambda · Glue · Athena · ETL</p>
		</a>

		<a class="project-card" href="/projects/musicstream-analytics-pipeline">
			<img src="/projects/musicstream-pipeline.jpg" alt="MusicStream pipeline analysis">
			<h3>MusicStream Analytics Pipeline</h3>
			<p>Built an end-to-end music analytics pipeline integrating Spotify and Last.fm APIs, Python ETL workflows, 
				and MySQL to analyze artist popularity and genre trends.</p>
			<p class="tools">Python · APIs · ETL · MySQL</p>
		</a>

		<a class="project-card" href="/projects/world-happiness-report">
			<img src="/projects/world-happiness-dashboard.jpg" alt="World Happiness dashboard">
			<h3>World Happiness Report Dashboard</h3>
			<p>Explored global well-being indicators through Python ETL workflows and 
				interactive Power BI dashboards using World Happiness Report data.</p>
			<p class="tools">Python · ETL · Power BI</p>
		</a>

		<a class="project-card" href="/projects/employee-retention-analysis">
			<img src="/projects/employee-retention-analysis.jpg" alt="Employee retention analysis">
			<h3>Employee Retention Analysis</h3>
			<p>Performed exploratory analysis of HR survey data using Python to evaluate employee retention 
				patterns, satisfaction metrics, and data quality.</p>
			<p class="tools">Python · Data Cleaning · EDA · Visualization</p>
		</a>

		<a class="project-card" href="/projects/friends-analytics-dashboard">
			<img src="/projects/friends-tableau-dashboard.jpg" alt="Friends Tableau dashboard">
			<h3>Friends Analytics Dashboard</h3>
			<p>Designed an interactive Tableau dashboard analyzing ratings, viewership, and episode-level 
				trends across all ten seasons of Friends.</p>
			<p class="tools">Tableau · Data Visualization · Storytelling · Data Cleaning</p>
		</a>

		</div>
	</div>
	</section>

    </main>
  </body>
</html>